Z||000001||rogergarrison||08-31-2001||09:54 PM||||Just like a convertible conversion, it takes too much work to reenforce the floor. Fiero has no frame except front and back so a car will just bend down in the middle if you take out the top. T-tops still have a center beam to keep that from happening, but they still have a lot of squeeks and rattles from twisting.||||reg||1
Z||000002||cadaver||08-31-2001||10:17 PM||||Reinforcing a fiero for a top off car is not that big a deal. If you lived close I would do it for you.||||reg||1
